menu "HSN firmware"

    config HSN_DEVELOPMENT_BUILD
        bool "Development build"
        default y
        help
            A development build accepts Provision and Erase at any time and Set role whenever it
            is sent, and says so in its identity (protocol section 10, PR5). M1b's bench boards
            are development builds; a release build turns this off.

    config HSN_LOG_EVENTS
        bool "Print every radio event and packet on the console"
        default n
        help
            Raises the waiter's own log tag to debug at start-up, so each radio event (its kind,
            time, size, RSSI and SNR) and each link packet's size is printed on UART0. It needs
            CONFIG_LOG_MAXIMUM_LEVEL_DEBUG, which sdkconfig.bench sets with this. For the bench
            only: printing costs time on every event.

endmenu
